Package: certhaven
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: tvjay <11197859+tvjay@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/tvjay/certhaven
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-flask (>= 3.0), python3-flask-sqlalchemy (>= 3.1), python3-sqlalchemy (>= 2.0), python3-cryptography (>= 42), python3-werkzeug (>= 3.0), python3-click, python3-markupsafe, gunicorn (>= 22), nginx, openssl, adduser, systemd
Recommends: unattended-upgrades, ufw
Conflicts: certmgr
Replaces: certmgr
Description: self-hosted private certificate authority with a web UI
 certhaven is a certificate manager that runs as a web application.
 It builds root and intermediate CA hierarchies, issues certificates from
 templates, signs CSRs, revokes certificates and publishes CRLs at public
 URLs, and imports and exports PEM, DER and PKCS#12.
 .
 Users have Admin, Operator or Auditor roles and every action is recorded in
 an audit log. Private keys are encrypted at rest with a key wrapped by each
 key holder's password. Email alerts warn about expiring certificates, CRLs
 and failed logins.
 .
 The package runs certhaven under gunicorn behind nginx, with sandboxed
 systemd units, a nightly backup timer and an email-alert timer.
